\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RPropsubst13
\item[* relevant examples:] x1 "graag" x2 + x1 compra libros $\rightarrow$
x1 compra "graag" libros; 
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-Rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoClause
\item[* class:] Proposition Substitution
\item[* date of creation:] 18-DEC-1987 11:00:00  
\item[* author:] Lisetta Appelo, Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 30/09/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:]
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
There is a subrule for NPVARs and CNVARs
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
See documents on graag-like by Jan Odijk; doc. on subgrammars by Lisette Appelo
and Carel Fellinger
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
This rule is between comment-brackets for Spanish at this moment!
\item modifications: OPENVERBPPROP is substituted by SENTENCE. Order in model 
reversed. Attributes and values adapted.\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}



